Task: Stop a Places miss from erasing coordinates (D5) — Phase 1

Summary of changes
- scripts/enrich_maps_data.py: MERGE now sets latitude/longitude via
  IFNULL(S.x, T.x) instead of assigning the incoming value unconditionally.
- scripts/test_enrich_maps_data.py (new): first tests for this script. Covers
  the Places miss, a hit with a location, and a hit with no location block.
- cloudbuild.yaml: test step runs 'pytest app/ scripts/'.

Why
The miss payload sets latitude/longitude to None and the MERGE wrote them
straight through, clearing any stored coordinates. Latent today because nothing
populates those columns; destructive once Phase 8 stores FSA Geocode at ingest.

Deviation from plan wording
The plan said to remove latitude/longitude from the miss payload. That is not
workable: the payload feeds a positional STRUCT whose field list must stay
intact. Guarding in the MERGE is the correct fix and additionally covers a
Places hit that returns no location, which the plan had not identified.

Verification
pytest app/ scripts/ -> 90 passed. Red phase confirmed 2 failures first.
requirements.txt already carries requests and google-cloud-bigquery, and the
module creates no BigQuery client at import, so the widened CI step stays
offline.
